# --- build and dependency output -------------------------------------------
# `build/` was previously listed here as a generic output pattern, but nothing
# in this repository ever writes to a directory literally named `build` — the
# real compiled output is `dist/`, already covered below. As an unanchored
# pattern, `build/` silently matched `tests/build/` too, which is a real
# source directory (the child-process build tests), not generated output. It
# was never tracked, never committed, and CI's "Child-process build tests"
# step failed with "No test files found" as a result. See A57.
node_modules/
dist/
.next/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- generated and diagnostic artifacts -------------------------------------
stress-logs/
graphify-out/
.smart-env/

# --- secrets and local state -------------------------------------------------
# Telga never generates or stores TLS key material, and no .env is used by the
# application. These patterns exist so an accidentally created one cannot be
# published — see `09 Engineering/Local Certificate Handling.md`.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# --- editor, agent and plugin configuration ---------------------------------
# Personal to this machine, ~19 MB of third-party plugin bundles, and four
# duplicate copies of the same agent skill set. None of it is needed to build,
# test or run Telga.
.obsidian/
.agents/
.claude/
.opencode/
copilot/

# --- commercial and strategic material ---------------------------------------
# Business strategy, provider assessment, engagement records, agreement terms,
# pilot budget and merchant selection. None of it is required by the source,
# tests, build, CI or runtime. Publishing it — even to a private repository — is
# an irreversible disclosure to a third party, and would weaken MuleSoo's
# position before a single agreement exists.
#
# It stays in the vault on this machine. `npm run docs:validate` enforces the
# boundary: a published note that links to one, or names a file inside one, is a
# failure rather than a warning.
docs/obsidian/01 Strategy/
docs/obsidian/06 Partnerships/
docs/obsidian/08 Pilot/
docs/obsidian/00 Home (Local).md

# --- source material and personal workspace files ---------------------------
# The founder's source PDF, and Obsidian's default scratch files.
CLAUDE.pdf
Untitled.canvas
Welcome.md

# --- Android signing and machine-specific build state -----------------------
# A release keystore signs every Telga update. Google Play ties an app's
# identity to it: lose it and no update can ever be published for that listing
# again; leak it and somebody else can sign something that installs as Telga.
# It is a real secret in the sense of CLAUDE.md §24, and it must never enter
# this repository — not even a private one.
*.jks
*.keystore
apps/mobile/android/keystore.properties
apps/mobile/android/local.properties

# Generated from apps/mobile/shell.config.json by `npm run mobile:configure`.
# Committing it would let a stale copy contradict the file that owns the list.
apps/mobile/www/config.js

# Capacitor copies the web assets in here on every sync; the source is www/.
apps/mobile/android/app/src/main/assets/public/
apps/mobile/android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.config.json
apps/mobile/android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.plugins.json

# SQLite writes three files, not one. `*.sqlite` alone let the write-ahead log
# and shared-memory file through, and those hold real training ledger data.
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Backup output and its manifests are operational artifacts, not source.
backups/
*.sqlite.manifest.json

# --- Scanned documents and screenshots -------------------------------------
#
# A 2 MB Adobe Scan sat untracked at the root of this repository. Nobody opened
# it to find out what it held, and that is the point: this project handles
# trade licences and owner identity documents, §18.1 refuses photograph uploads
# outright, and a scan pushed to a remote is in the history permanently even
# after it is deleted. Scans and screenshots go nowhere near the repository.
*.pdf
!docs/**/*.pdf
Adobe Scan*.pdf
gpt.png
*.screenshot.png

# --- Scratch ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `verify-training.cjs` is a stale one-off: it selects on `merchant_key`, a
# column no migration creates, so it throws; it asserts migration 007 when the
# schema is at 022; and it sums `amount_minor` without reading `direction`,
# which on a double-entry ledger produces a figure that means nothing. Left on
# disk for its author to remove, kept out of the repository so nobody runs it
# and trusts the number.
verify-training.cjs
docs/fs-read-write-writev.md

# Design review captures are disposable evidence, regenerated on demand. The
# token sidecar and the surface briefs are not: later sessions reload them.
.impeccable/review/
.impeccable/mocks/

# Decision-page transcripts: one session's question-and-answer log, superseded
# by the Decision Log entry the choice produced.
.impeccable/questions/
